<Policy title="Corrections and update policy" description="Report factual or calculation errors in The MoneyGoal guides and read our correction history, source-review process and publication hold policy.">
<p>Financial explanations can become inaccurate or outdated. We correct material mistakes, identify meaningful changes and preserve the distinction between a new fact and an editorial correction.</p>
<h2>Report a problem</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/yojika-systems/the-money-goal/issues/new?template=correction.yml">Open a public correction report</a> with the page URL, disputed statement and supporting primary document. A GitHub account is required. Do not include account numbers, identity documents or private financial details.</p>
<h2>How corrections are handled</h2><p>A confirmed error is corrected in the page and its update date. Material errors are listed below. Affected promotions are withheld if their terms cannot be verified. If an automated release fails its checks, publication stops; deployment failures trigger recovery checks before rollback.</p>
<h2>Correction history</h2><ul><li><strong>17 November 2026:</strong> Corrected the expense-ratio article’s worked table to match its stated monthly contribution and nominal-return assumptions. Removed the shared claim that direct mutual fund purchases require a demat account. Sources now point to specific AMFI documents.</li><li><strong>17 November 2026:</strong> Revised mutual-fund risk descriptions and the financial-independence guide to remove implied safety or indefinite portfolio sustainability. Removed daily and twelve-language publishing promises that did not match the archive.</li></ul>
</Policy>
